  "description": {
    "text": "The Lizardon Mega Battle of 2014 was Japan's spring championship, named after the 1997-98 series: an East Japan tournament at Pacifico Yokohama on 3 and 4 May 2014 and a West Japan tournament at Intex Osaka on 17 and 18 May, with qualifying rounds on the first day and the main tournament on the second, then a Japan Championship at Pokémon Center Osaka on 7 and 8 June whose top finishers were invited to the 2014 World Championships. Clearing a block of the qualifying round earned a Protection Cube, and the top three of each league won Victory Ring in gold, silver or bronze stamped with the event's logo. Side events on the first day gave a holo Blacksmith for three straight wins in the Triple Beat Battle and a holo Fire Energy for each team win in the 5 on 5 Battle; Play Points from the second day's side events bought prizes such as Greninja. Mega Pack \"Lizardon Mega Battle\" marked it in April.",
